{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact GS-1 head eb3b59d31e5472893ce64bee752bef55aae0e220, tree 2b5e4eebfd21f5a9ae679d2dccfa041697b7bd15, on builder/gs1-short-gate-20261114, all 36 artifacts, for request 89bdceee under implementation promise f3d79f87 and my promise a4720c2e. The head writes rulings f45b355a and 13ea7ab7 into the docs, skips `npm test` only for a head that changes nothing outside `notes/`, and moves 16 Native cases into the scale tier without changing a case body.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `scripts/gate-test-selection.mjs`. `gateTestSelection` resolves both commits, requires the base to be an ancestor, and reads the whole base-to-head diff with `--no-renames` and `-z`. `gateTestDecision` skips only when the list is nonempty and every path starts with `notes/`. A missing base, a bad ref, a non-ancestor or incomplete output exits 2, and `gate.sh` treats exit 2 and any unexpected answer as a failure. A move from source into `notes/` keeps the old path in the list, so it runs the tests. Every other gate step still runs on a notes-only head.\n- `scripts/gate.sh`. The gate runs `check-notes.test.mjs` and the selection owner before the test step, and `scripts/test.mjs` drops `check-notes.test.mjs` from `nodeFiles`, so a full gate runs that owner once.\n- The moved cases. For each of the five mixed owners, I compared the main file with its new `.fixture.ts`. Every non-import line of the old file appears in the fixture. The only added lines are the two `register…` wrappers, one `describe` repeated for the demo split, and the `scenarios` parameter of `registerArchiveInstalledCases`. The ordinary and scale `archive-installed` entries split the nine original scenarios eight to one, with \"Grow production\" in scale. The four sole-case owners do not change.\n- The scale wiring. `vitest.scale-files.ts` names 13 owners with their case counts, 22 in all. `scale-runner.mjs` now checks each owner's count as well as the total. `vitest.worker.config.ts` and the `scope-stories` project exclude all 13 owners, so no case runs in two projects. `scope-scale` gains the same `provide` values as the story project.\n- `scripts/scale-selection.mjs`. The protected set adds the scale owners, the shared fixtures and the production paths that the moved cases cover, as the note's table lists. `scale-runner.mjs` joins the selection files.\n- The corpus and inventory edits. They change only the moved manifest fixture path.\n- `scripts/check-notes.mjs`. The edit removes the warning for a new evidence file name and keeps the size warning.\n- The docs. `docs/evidence-filing.md` and `docs/testing.md` state the one-log record, no power condition, no seal, manifest or checksum file, and the notes-only skip as the code does.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 270dc8c7 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The 36 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 270dc8c7 eb3b59d3`.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-gs1-gate-attempt3/gate.log` has SHA-256 bae19caa…, as the note states. Its first lines name head 5d296e17 and tree 63669bfb with 0 changed files. Its last gate line is \"gate passed\", and the three `time` lines follow it. The three cited control files beside it match the note's digests. From 5d296e17 to the head only the GS-1 note changes, so the documentation-only follow-up rule applies.\n- No case lost or doubled. The gate counts Plain 4715 passed and 1 skipped, and Native 1156 passed and 2 skipped. Combined gate attempt 2 at 1c80cef3 had the same counts, and it also ran the scale tier.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 10 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The skip decision reads the whole range and fails closed, and each moved case keeps its body, deadline and worker limits. The per-owner count in the runner closes the gap where one missing case could hide behind an extra one.\n\nOne fact for the timing record. The note compares with the R2 Grow gate, whose selector omitted the scale tier. Combined gate attempt 2 at 1c80cef3 ran the scale tier with four owners, and its Native step took 1539.87 seconds. GS-1's Native step, with 22 scale cases, took 1337.53 seconds. These are still different heads, so neither pair shows a cause. The saving that GS-1 aims at appears only on a head whose selector omits scale. The protected set includes files that many heads edit: `packages/scope/src/core.ts`, `sqlite.ts`, `operations.ts`, `worker.ts`, `packages/derive/src/judge.ts`, `fold.ts`, `packages/platform/src/destination.ts`, `packages/scope/test/fixtures.ts` and `support.ts`. A head that touches any of them runs all 22 scale cases.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Only a range that changes nothing outside `notes/` skips the test step. Dependency verification, whitespace, commit, citation, note, format, typecheck and definition-pin steps still run. The head changes no product source and no protected model function.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The fixtures share one body between the ordinary and scale entries, so no case has two copies.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing, push or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fcc675964bfcd7bf00dc1c0bf24b0c27ec0c9378","binding":"assigned","head":"eb3b59d31e5472893ce64bee752bef55aae0e220","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a4720c2e739dc3c299bf32256d1923bba24df769\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f3d79f874bd82a5b6d0b3d106912e8048bf1c16d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6175c3c16e9cea79e3b2745c25c763e5077212f8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0087e528c5c6178ec9d36437511ac12f23c